# Press the overview map's staircase keys and record what they choose. This
# is the oracle for two changes made on 2026-08-20: the fix that let '<' and
# '>' reach the staircase search at all (inc-pw1.5), and the change that made
# the search offer staircases in the order they cost to walk to (inc-pw1.4).
#
#   INCURSION_STAIR_PROBE=1 tools/headless.sh tools/keys/stair-cycle.keys 1
#
# Read the result with tools/check_stair_cycle.sh, which is what asserts on
# the probe log. This file only produces the log.
#
# THE ROUTE IN IS [l] THEN [o], AND [o] ALONE DOES NOT WORK. In play mode
# GetCharCmd walks the keyset backwards (src/Wposix.cpp:1270), so 'o' reaches
# KY_CMD_OPEN at src/Tables.cpp:4636 and never KY_CMD_OVERVIEW_MAP at :4616.
# In the Look prompt it walks forwards and finds the overview entry first.
# Both keysets are built the same way, so the map has one route in.
#
# Every letter here is lowercase on purpose. TokenToKey (src/Wposix.cpp:892)
# sets SHIFT for an uppercase token, and these bindings demand no modifier,
# so 'O' matches nothing at all.
#
# '<' comes before '>' because seed 1 knows an ascending staircase on arrival
# and no descending one. A press that finds nothing opens a message box, and
# the box eats the next key; putting the fruitless presses last keeps that
# from swallowing the presses the check wants to read.
#
# ponytail: seed 1 knows exactly ONE staircase of each kind, so this session
# proves the search runs, proves the choice is the cheapest candidate, and
# proves the cursor wraps -- but it cannot prove the ORDER of two candidates,
# because it never has two. To lift that ceiling the session needs a level
# where the character remembers two staircases of one kind. A blind walk does
# not get there: the character stays boxed in the entry chamber, and 55
# rounds of the map's own Tab-then-Run explore did not either. A potion or
# spell of detect stairs would do it in one keystroke, and the wizard menu
# can conjure one ([w] y [e]), but its acquisition prompt is an interactive
# picker that this key format cannot drive yet.

@include chargen.keys

# A few turns so the level settles, then a short walk away from the arrival
# staircase. The walk matters: standing on the staircase makes its path cost
# zero, and a zero tells the check nothing about whether the cost is real.
.*3
DOWN*4 LEFT*4
@dump:arrival

l o                 # Look, then the overview map
<*6                 # ascending staircases: more presses than the level has
>*6                 # descending staircases: seed 1 knows none of these
ESC
@dump:left-the-map

@quit
